member.summary:
Handles a decrypted, signature-verified inbound document.
Keep the work fast — NPS expects an immediate HTTP 200 acknowledgment;
offload long-running processing to a queue or background job.

When true, uses AES-256-GCM for outbound payload encryption; otherwise AES-256-CBC
(the algorithm shown in the guide's .NET encryption sample). NIBSS responses use GCM;
both are always supported for inbound decryption.

Identification types accepted in the NPS supplementary data
(Debtor/Creditor Info IdType). Per the guide: if NIN, account tier must be 1;
JTBTIN / FIRSTIN / RC Number require a corporate account designation.
